# oracle: w303vsplit_pppm — run_style verlet/split on two partitions with kspace_style pppm (64 ions, real units): the Rspace partition prints the thermo of run_style verlet; the Kspace partition prints no thermo and ends the run with the Rspace partition's coordinates and its own velocities (its atoms are not compared: native copies the coordinates in its spatially sorted local order, so they land on other atom IDs)
# oracle-partitions: 2
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomparts=0
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms of partition 1): thermo 1.8e-14, atoms 1.7e-12.
units           real
atom_style      charge
atom_modify     map array
lattice         sc 2.8
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 22.99
set             type 1 charge 1.0
set             group all type/fraction 2 0.5 12345
set             type 2 charge -1.0
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long 8.0
pair_coeff      * * 0.1 2.5
kspace_style    pppm 1.0e-5
velocity        all create 300 4928459
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run_style       verlet/split
run             100
